  "summary": "EFF celebrates Austin's decision not to renew its Flock Safety ALPR contract after a coalition of 30+ community groups pushed back. An audit revealed over 20% of APD's ALPR searches lacked proper documentation and that contract terms violated council-mandated retention limits. Austin still uses Axon ALPRs.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "This successful pushback from the community means at the end of the month Austin police will no longer be able to use the surveillance network of automated license plate readers (ALPRs) across the city.",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "an audit of the Austin Police Department program also revealed that over 20% of ALPR database searches lacked proper documentation or justification, in violation of department policy.",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "While the Flock contract has been discontinued, Austin still makes use of ALPRs via its contract with Axon",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    }
  ],
